@preamble let store = import("store")
new
Creates explicit mutable indexed storage with size cells. Each cell is
initialized to 0. A store is intended for systems work that requires
mutation; ordinary Aiki lists remain immutable. A store may be shared between
spawned computations by passing it explicitly as an argument. Spawn does not
capture outer bindings, so shared mutable access must be explicit in the
program.

new(size)

let memory = store.new(1024)
store.length(memory)    # 1024
===
get
Returns the value stored at index. Indexing is zero-based. An index outside
the store faults.

get(store, index)

let memory = store.new(4)
store.get(memory, 0)    # 0
===
set
Replaces the value at index. The store is changed in place and set returns [].
An index outside the store faults.

set(store, index, value)

let memory = store.new(4)
store.set(memory, 2, 7094)    # []
store.get(memory, 2)    # 7094
===
length
Returns the number of cells in a store.

length(store)

let memory = store.new(36)
store.length(memory)    # 36

===
snapshot
Returns an immutable Aiki list containing a point-in-time copy of the store.
With an optional count, only the first count cells are copied. This is useful
when Store is used as an explicit mutable accumulation buffer and an immutable
list is required at the boundary.

snapshot(store, ...args)

let memory = store.new(4)
let ignored0 = store.set(memory, 0, 10)
let ignored1 = store.set(memory, 1, 20)
store.snapshot(memory, 2)    # [10, 20]

===
digits_to_text
Encodes a store containing integer digits 0-9 into a string. With an optional
count, only the first count cells are encoded.

digits_to_text(store, ...args)

let memory = store.new(4)
let ignored0 = store.set(memory, 0, 1)
let ignored1 = store.set(memory, 1, 2)
let ignored2 = store.set(memory, 2, 3)
store.digits_to_text(memory, 3)    # "123"

===
checksum
Computes the standard dense-store checksum used by diagnostics over all cells
or the first count cells. The checksum starts at 17 and updates with
((value * 131) + cell + index) modulo 1000000007.

checksum(store, ...args)

let memory = store.new(3)
let ignored0 = store.set(memory, 0, 1)
let ignored1 = store.set(memory, 1, 0)
let ignored2 = store.set(memory, 2, 1)
store.checksum(memory, 3)    # 38234842
